====== Leetcode 90. Subsets II =======

Step-by-step algorithm to generate all subsets of an array with duplicates handled:

Step 1: Sort the input array nums.

Sorting ensures that duplicate numbers are next to each other, which helps in skipping them later.

Step 2: Initialize an empty list al to store all subsets.

Step 3: Call a recursive function find starting from index 0 with an empty temporary list arl.

Step 4: In the recursive function find:

Sub-step 4a: Add a copy of the current list arl to al.
(This stores the current subset.)

Sub-step 4b: Loop over the elements from st (current start index) to n-1:

Sub-sub-step 4b-i: Skip duplicates:
If i > st and nums[i] == nums[i-1], continue to the next iteration.
(This avoids generating the same subset multiple times.)

Sub-sub-step 4b-ii: Add the current element nums[i] to arl.

Sub-sub-step 4b-iii: Recursively call find with the next index i + 1.
(This explores all subsets including the current element.)

Sub-sub-step 4b-iv: Remove the last element from arl.
(This backtracks to explore subsets without the current element.)

Step 5: Continue the recursion until all elements are considered.

Step 6: Return al containing all unique subsets.

Time Complexity:
There are up to 2^n possible subsets.
Each subset can take O(n) time to copy.
Time Complexity = O(n × 2^n)

Space Complexity:
Recursive call stack can go up to n levels.
Space Complexity = O(n) (excluding the output list)


        -----------------> Code <-------------------

class Solution {
    List<List<Integer>> al=new ArrayList<>();
    public List<List<Integer>> subsetsWithDup(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        find(nums,0,nums.length,new ArrayList<>());
        return al;
    }
    public void find(int[] nums,int st,int n,List<Integer> arl){
        al.add(new ArrayList<>(arl));
        
        for(int i=st;i<n;i++){

            if(i>st && nums[i]==nums[i-1])continue;
            
            arl.add(nums[i]);
            find(nums,i+1,n,arl);
            arl.remove(arl.size()-1);
        }
    }
}
